WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.670
True to the spirit of everyone's favorite
regenerating degenerate, Deadpool 2 doesn't

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:09.170
hold back on the violence, profanity, and
fourth-wall-breaks, taking everything great

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.760
about the first movie and turning it up to
11.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.760
In that vein, Deadpool 2 also introduced a
ton of new characters, and then...well, let's

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.689
just say there are plenty of spoilers ahead.

00:00:19.689 --> 00:00:23.310
Some of those new characters carry a lot of
weight in the comics...and a few have even

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.110
saved the world once or twice.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:29.929
Let's take a look at all the characters in
Deadpool 2 who mean more than you realized.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.460
Zeitgeist

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.530
A lot of hype was given to all the new mutants
debuting in Deadpool 2.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.530
Then the movie came out and dispatched them
all in horrible ways before they even got

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:41.079
to their first mission.

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:45.710
Which is a shame, because some of those characters
have insane stories in the comics.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:49.010
Take Zeitgeist, played in the film by Bill
Skarsgard.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:53.410
Once upon a time, he was actually the leader
of one incarnation of the X-Force.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.590
And boy, were they weird.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:01:01.210
After 115 generally solid issues of X-Force,
the series took a bizarre left turn.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:06.930
As issue #116 opens, a drunk 14-year-old vomits
acid all over a girl's face when he tries

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:07.930
to kiss her.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:12.750
Flash forward in time, and he's Zeitgeist,
the leader of a new X-Force.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.530
They all seem to be drunk most of the time,
at least when they're not groping each other

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.040
or doing drugs.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:22.340
Figuring the team needs a little good press,
Zeitgeist hires a group of terrorists to kidnap

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.130
a pop band called Boyz R Us.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:29.980
X-Force teleports to the scene and obliterates
all the bad guys, and then Zeitgeist and most

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.409
of the team get cut to pieces and die.

00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:33.450
The end.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.080
Is it a weird chapter in X-Force's history
books?

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.390
Oh, you bet.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:41.630
But somehow, Zeitgeist feels exactly like
the right type of person to add to a Deadpool

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:47.290
movie - and technically, they followed his
story pretty closely, all the way to the woodchipper

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:48.350
end.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.560
Bedlam

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.579
Ever since his official introduction as Bedlam
in the pages of X-Force #82, Jesse Aaronson

00:01:54.579 --> 00:01:57.770
has been one of the core members of the crime-fighting
team.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:02.469
As a mutant with the ability to influence
electronics through his own bioelectric field,

00:02:02.469 --> 00:02:05.909
Bedlam definitely played a pivotal role in
several missions.

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:10.009
And like he says in the movie, he really can
directly affect people's brains, which came

00:02:10.009 --> 00:02:14.370
in handy when the citizens of San Francisco
were turned into brainwashed zombies and Bedlam

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:17.540
was able to reverse the brainwashing without
destroying them all.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:21.310
But once upon a time, Bedlam almost destroyed
the planet.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:26.470
In X-Force #87, Bedlam left the X-Force to
join up with his long lost brother, Christopher,

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:29.069
on a team called the New Hellions.

00:02:29.069 --> 00:02:33.870
Bedlam later finds out that, in a series of
jerk moves, Christopher had killed their parents

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:38.739
14 years earlier and was now planning to revive
a mutant named Armageddon Man with the power

00:02:38.739 --> 00:02:40.610
to sweep the world with natural disasters.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:44.129
In other words, it was a bad family reunion.

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:49.410
Realizing the error of his ways, Bedlam rejoins
X-Force to put a stop to Armageddon Man, and

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:52.590
they all learn a valuable lesson about friendship.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:53.590
Vanisher

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:58.569
You don't see a lot of Vanisher in Deadpool
2, which makes Brad Pitt's eventual cameo

00:02:58.569 --> 00:02:59.480
all the more shocking.

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:06.720
The Vanisher of the comics is much different
than the one we see - or rather, don't see

00:03:06.739 --> 00:03:08.190
- in the movie.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:14.349
First gracing the pages of Uncanny X-Men #2,
the Vanisher was one of the OG X-Men foes,

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:18.560
a teleporting mutant who liked to rob banks
and steal government secrets.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:23.080
Decades later, Vanisher was still living a
life of crime when X-Force tracked him down,

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:27.830
gave him a brain tumor, and forced him to
teleport them around to their battles, essentially

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:30.349
turning him into their indentured slave.

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:35.599
In a long career filled with dark moments,
this was definitely one of the X-Force's darkest,

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:39.060
and it proved that they were willing to go
to any lengths to get a job done.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.650
No wonder Deadpool likes them so much.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.440
Black Tom Cassidy

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:47.879
Black Tom Cassidy's biggest contribution in
Deadpool 2 is giving Deadpool an excuse to

00:03:47.879 --> 00:03:50.379
grief Cable over who he chooses to shoot.

00:03:50.379 --> 00:03:52.989
But in the comics, he has a much bigger role.

00:03:52.989 --> 00:03:58.239
Black Tom is a mutant infected with the same
techno-organic virus that affects Cable.

00:03:58.239 --> 00:04:02.689
Just like in the movie, Black Tom was incarcerated
at the same prison as Juggernaut, and he was

00:04:02.689 --> 00:04:04.440
also shot by Cable.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:08.660
Here's where the two paths diverge, however
- in the comics, after Cable shoots him, Black

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:14.239
Tom gets healed and gains the ability to control
plants - because why not? - and also gains

00:04:14.239 --> 00:04:16.150
Deadpool's healing factor.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:20.220
That's exactly the kind of villain that could
come back to haunt Deadpool, especially if

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:25.710
another Deadpool movie takes up the recent
Avengers theme of "everything we do has consequences."

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.500
But maybe without the plant thing.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.070
That might be too weird, even by Deadpool
standards.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.270
Russell

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:37.979
Since Deadpool 2 basically served as the origin
story for Russell Collins, AKA Firefist, it

00:04:37.979 --> 00:04:40.790
made sure to hit some of the character's notes
from the comics.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:46.190
Firefist's origin story saw him as a Navy
recruit who suddenly discovers his fiery powers,

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:48.410
gets locked up, and breaks free.

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:51.620
X-Factor shows up to fight him, then lets
him join the team.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:56.560
And then, in the events leading up to X-Force
#24, Russell is imprisoned by a mutant-hating

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.949
group called the Friends of Humanity, leading
the X-Force to mount a rescue operation while

00:05:00.949 --> 00:05:05.770
he's in transit - pretty much what happened
in Deadpool 2, but with fewer crotches landing

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:07.090
on Cable's face.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:11.830
But his biggest contributions to X-Force have
been, well, giving them something to fight.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:16.101
Not once, but twice has he been brainwashed
and turned to the dark side in the comics

00:05:16.101 --> 00:05:19.070
- once for every finger he can give.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:22.900
We're not sure where his character will go
in any upcoming films, but one thing's for

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:26.870
sure - they sure picked a hell of a kid to
rescue.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:28.289
Domino

00:05:28.289 --> 00:05:32.700
When you break it right down, Domino has some
of the most useful powers in the whole film,

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.830
and she's used them plenty of times in the
comics to get both Deadpool and Cable out

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:38.110
of tight spots.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:40.490
She also gets one of the coolest sequences
in the movie.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:45.870
When she wants to, she can even get the best
of Deadpool with just a few well-timed words,

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:48.729
which makes her one of the most formidable
mutants on the team.

00:05:48.729 --> 00:05:53.430
Any future Deadpool film is bound to feature
a ton of Domino showing off how powerful she

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:54.680
really is.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:57.860
And despite what Deadpool may say about it,
that's a pretty useful ability.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:58.920
"Yes it is."

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:01.380
"Let's meet in the middle and say no it isn't."

00:06:01.389 --> 00:06:02.389
Hope Summers

00:06:02.389 --> 00:06:06.940
Leave it to Deadpool to introduce one of the
most powerful mutants in the world and then

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:09.400
end her brief story so tragically.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:13.680
We're talking about Hope Summers, of course
- Cable's daughter and the whole reason he

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.919
traveled back in time in the first place.

00:06:15.919 --> 00:06:22.169
In the comics, Hope is what's known as an
Omega-level mutant - basically just unstoppably

00:06:22.169 --> 00:06:23.169
powerful.

00:06:23.169 --> 00:06:28.680
After Cyclops becomes Dark Phoenix in Avengers
vs. X-Men #11, Hope harnesses the Phoenix

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:32.319
Force to become an even more powerful Phoenix
and stop him.

00:06:32.319 --> 00:06:38.370
And in Uncanny X-Men #541, Hope absorbs all
of the X-Men's powers to put a stop to an

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.380
out-of-control Juggernaut.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:41.400
Where does it end?

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:48.080
Well, in X-Men Legacy #263, she admits that
she's never seen the true limits of her powers.

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:52.210
Now that Cable successfully stopped her death,
Hope Summers could have a big role to play

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:56.240
in whatever on-screen form the X-Force takes
next.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.349
Yukio and Shatterstar

00:06:58.349 --> 00:07:02.389
In the film, Shatterstar is a sword-wielding
mutant from Mojoworld.

00:07:02.389 --> 00:07:06.819
In the comics, he's also a sword-wielding
mutant from Mojoworld, along with some extra

00:07:06.819 --> 00:07:11.509
weirdness that made him his own dad's father,
but that's not where we're going here.

00:07:11.509 --> 00:07:16.530
After a long history in the comics, X-Factor
#45 had Shatterstar come out as gay and featured

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:20.380
a panel of him and fellow male mutant Rictor
locking lips.

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:25.080
The internet was quick to praise the writers
of Deadpool 2 for featuring a gay superhero.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.990
But now that the movie is out and the only
thing Shatterstar shattered were some helicopter

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:34.630
blades, all the attention in that arena falls
on Yukio, who is now in an onscreen relationship

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.910
with Negasonic Teenage Warhead.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:42.640
While Marvel movies have technically featured
LGBTQ characters before, Deadpool 2 puts that

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:47.370
representation right in the forefront, but
only after making everyone think it was going

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:48.970
to come from somewhere else.

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:50.400
That's pure Deadpool.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.400
Thanks for watching!

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.090
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:56.240
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

